WEBVTT

00:00:00.673 --> 00:00:02.248
Command of evidence.

00:00:02.248 --> 00:00:03.933
Split the claim into parts.

00:00:03.933 --> 00:00:06.147
The evidence has to hit every part.

00:00:07.677 --> 00:00:09.377
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:09.377 --> 00:00:12.777
The passage gives a claim, or a hypothesis.

00:00:12.777 --> 00:00:17.475
And the question asks which finding would most directly support it, or weaken it.

00:00:18.493 --> 00:00:21.269
It's testing what actually counts as evidence.

00:00:22.336 --> 00:00:23.556
Here's the method.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.156
Find the exact claim.

00:00:25.156 --> 00:00:28.576
It's often the last sentence, or the hypothesis.

00:00:28.576 --> 00:00:30.326
Split it into its parts.

00:00:30.326 --> 00:00:33.636
Decide: do you need support, or weaken?

00:00:33.636 --> 00:00:37.208
Then pick the choice that hits every part, in the right direction.

00:00:38.294 --> 00:00:39.944
Four evidence rules.

00:00:39.944 --> 00:00:43.769
Support means the result the claim predicts actually happens.

00:00:43.769 --> 00:00:48.894
Weaken means the same result with a different cause, or the cause with no result.

00:00:48.894 --> 00:00:50.719
Half the claim isn't enough.

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:52.094
Hit every part.

00:00:52.094 --> 00:00:55.859
And for quotes from poems or novels, the literal meaning wins.

00:00:56.893 --> 00:00:58.068
Let's try one.

00:00:58.068 --> 00:01:04.068
The hypothesis: the lizards developed larger toe pads since the hurricane in twenty seventeen.

00:01:04.068 --> 00:01:07.808
Three parts: toe pads, bigger, and after the storm.

00:01:07.808 --> 00:01:09.273
A is about diet.

00:01:09.273 --> 00:01:11.148
C is about other species.

00:01:11.148 --> 00:01:13.848
D only confirms the winds were strong.

00:01:13.848 --> 00:01:16.248
None of them show these lizards changed.

00:01:16.248 --> 00:01:19.373
B shows bigger toe pads after the hurricane.

00:01:19.373 --> 00:01:20.750
It hits every part.

00:01:21.806 --> 00:01:24.956
Watch out for the right topic with the wrong claim.

00:01:24.956 --> 00:01:29.986
A choice can talk about the same lizards, or the same storm, and still prove nothing.

00:01:31.044 --> 00:01:32.929
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:32.929 --> 00:01:33.984
How to spot it.

00:01:33.984 --> 00:01:35.334
The four steps.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:36.879
The evidence rules.

00:01:36.879 --> 00:01:37.929
And the trap.

00:01:37.929 --> 00:01:40.716
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
